{"id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_TheBochnerTechnique#thm:pet-ch9-hodge-theorem","title":"thm:pet-ch9-hodge-theorem","path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_TheBochnerTechnique.md","line":70,"body":"","kind":"theorem","status":"not_started","tex":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_TheBochnerTechnique.tex#thm:pet-ch9-hodge-theorem","uses":["[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_TheBochnerTechnique#def:pet-ch9-hodge-cohomology]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_TheBochnerTechnique#lem:pet-ch9-harmonic-iff-closed-coclosed]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_TheBochnerTechnique#def:pet-ch9-de-rham-cohomology]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_TheBochnerTechnique#thm:pet-ch9-hodge-theorem]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_TheBochnerTechnique#rem:pet-ch9-exercise-9-6-4]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_TheBochnerTechnique#rem:pet-ch9-exercise-9-6-5]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_TheBochnerTechnique.tex","label":"thm:pet-ch9-hodge-theorem","line":114,"source":"\\begin{theorem}[harmonic representatives for de Rham cohomology]\n  \\label{thm:pet-ch9-hodge-theorem}\n\n  \\source{petersen:page-0350}\n  \\uses{def:pet-ch9-hodge-cohomology, lem:pet-ch9-harmonic-iff-closed-coclosed, def:pet-ch9-de-rham-cohomology}\n  Every de Rham class on a closed oriented Riemannian manifold has exactly one\n  harmonic representative; equivalently,\n  $\\mathcal H^k(M)\\xrightarrow{\\sim}H^k(M)$.\n\\end{theorem}\n\\begin{proof}\n  \\uses{thm:pet-ch9-hodge-theorem,rem:pet-ch9-exercise-9-6-4,rem:pet-ch9-exercise-9-6-5}\n  \\sketch\n  The map is well defined and injective by\n  \\cref{lem:pet-ch9-harmonic-iff-closed-coclosed}.  Elliptic spectral theory,\n  developed in \\cref{rem:pet-ch9-exercise-9-6-4} and\n  \\cref{rem:pet-ch9-exercise-9-6-5}, yields\n  \\(\\Omega^k=\\operatorname{im}\\square\\oplus\\ker\\square\\).  Write a closed form as\n  \\(\\omega=d\\delta\\theta+\\delta d\\theta+\\widetilde\\omega\\), with\n  \\(\\square\\widetilde\\omega=0\\).  Applying \\(d\\) shows \\(d\\theta\\) is harmonic;\n  \\cref{lem:pet-ch9-harmonic-iff-closed-coclosed} then eliminates\n  \\(\\delta d\\theta\\).  Hence \\(\\omega\\) and \\(\\widetilde\\omega\\) are cohomologous.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Theorem</div></section>[harmonic representatives for de Rham cohomology] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-74686d3a7065742d6368392d686f6467652d7468656f72656d\"></span> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source\" style=\"display:block\">Source: <span class=\"reference\">petersen:page-0350</span></span> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh09_TheBochnerTechnique%23def%3Apet-ch9-hodge-cohomology\">↗ def:pet-ch9-hodge-cohomology</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh09_TheBochnerTechnique%23lem%3Apet-ch9-harmonic-iff-closed-coclosed\">↗ lem:pet-ch9-harmonic-iff-closed-coclosed</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh09_TheBochnerTechnique%23def%3Apet-ch9-de-rham-cohomology\">↗ def:pet-ch9-de-rham-cohomology</a> Every de Rham class on a closed oriented Riemannian manifold has exactly one harmonic representative; equivalently, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\mathcal H^k(M)\\xrightarrow {\\sim }H^k(M)$\">$\\mathcal H^k(M)\\xrightarrow {\\sim }H^k(M)$</span>.  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh09_TheBochnerTechnique%23thm%3Apet-ch9-hodge-theorem\">↗ thm:pet-ch9-hodge-theorem</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh09_TheBochnerTechnique%23rem%3Apet-ch9-exercise-9-6-4\">↗ rem:pet-ch9-exercise-9-6-4</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh09_TheBochnerTechnique%23rem%3Apet-ch9-exercise-9-6-5\">↗ rem:pet-ch9-exercise-9-6-5</a> \\sketch The map is well defined and injective by <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh09_TheBochnerTechnique%23lem%3Apet-ch9-harmonic-iff-closed-coclosed\" data-tex-node=\"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_TheBochnerTechnique#lem:pet-ch9-harmonic-iff-closed-coclosed\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a7065742d6368392d6861726d6f6e69632d6966662d636c6f7365642d636f636c6f736564\">section 1</a>. Elliptic spectral theory, developed in <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh09_TheBochnerTechnique%23rem%3Apet-ch9-exercise-9-6-4\" data-tex-node=\"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_TheBochnerTechnique#rem:pet-ch9-exercise-9-6-4\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-72656d3a7065742d6368392d65786572636973652d392d362d34\">section 5</a> and <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh09_TheBochnerTechnique%23rem%3Apet-ch9-exercise-9-6-5\" data-tex-node=\"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_TheBochnerTechnique#rem:pet-ch9-exercise-9-6-5\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-72656d3a7065742d6368392d65786572636973652d392d362d35\">item 3</a>, yields <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\Omega ^k=\\operatorname {im}\\square \\oplus \\ker \\square $\">$\\Omega ^k=\\operatorname {im}\\square \\oplus \\ker \\square $</span>. Write a closed form as <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\omega =d\\delta \\theta +\\delta d\\theta +\\widetilde\\omega $\">$\\omega =d\\delta \\theta +\\delta d\\theta +\\widetilde\\omega $</span>, with <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\square \\widetilde\\omega =0$\">$\\square \\widetilde\\omega =0$</span>. Applying <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$d$\">$d$</span> shows <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$d\\theta $\">$d\\theta $</span> is harmonic; <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh09_TheBochnerTechnique%23lem%3Apet-ch9-harmonic-iff-closed-coclosed\" data-tex-node=\"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_TheBochnerTechnique#lem:pet-ch9-harmonic-iff-closed-coclosed\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a7065742d6368392d6861726d6f6e69632d6966662d636c6f7365642d636f636c6f736564\">section 1</a> then eliminates <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\delta d\\theta $\">$\\delta d\\theta $</span>. Hence <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\omega $\">$\\omega $</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\widetilde\\omega $\">$\\widetilde\\omega $</span> are cohomologous. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_TheBochnerTechnique#def:pet-ch9-hodge-cohomology","next":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_TheBochnerTechnique#prop:pet-ch9-vector-field-1form-duality","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_TheBochnerTechnique#def:pet-ch9-hodge-cohomology","title":"def:pet-ch9-hodge-cohomology","label":"def:pet-ch9-hodge-cohomology"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_TheBochnerTechnique#lem:pet-ch9-harmonic-iff-closed-coclosed","title":"lem:pet-ch9-harmonic-iff-closed-coclosed","label":"lem:pet-ch9-harmonic-iff-closed-coclosed"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_TheBochnerTechnique#def:pet-ch9-de-rham-cohomology","title":"def:pet-ch9-de-rham-cohomology","label":"def:pet-ch9-de-rham-cohomology"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_TheBochnerTechnique#thm:pet-ch9-hodge-theorem","title":"thm:pet-ch9-hodge-theorem","label":"thm:pet-ch9-hodge-theorem"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_TheBochnerTechnique#rem:pet-ch9-exercise-9-6-4","title":"rem:pet-ch9-exercise-9-6-4","label":"rem:pet-ch9-exercise-9-6-4"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_TheBochnerTechnique#rem:pet-ch9-exercise-9-6-5","title":"rem:pet-ch9-exercise-9-6-5","label":"rem:pet-ch9-exercise-9-6-5"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_TheBochnerTechnique#thm:pet-ch9-hodge-theorem","title":"thm:pet-ch9-hodge-theorem","label":"thm:pet-ch9-hodge-theorem"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_TheBochnerTechnique#rem:pet-ch9-exercise-9-6-14","title":"rem:pet-ch9-exercise-9-6-14","label":"rem:pet-ch9-exercise-9-6-14"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_TheBochnerTechnique#thm:pet-ch9-hodge-theorem","title":"thm:pet-ch9-hodge-theorem","tex":"\\begin{theorem}[harmonic representatives for de Rham cohomology]\n  \\label{thm:pet-ch9-hodge-theorem}\n\n  \\source{petersen:page-0350}\n  \\uses{def:pet-ch9-hodge-cohomology, lem:pet-ch9-harmonic-iff-closed-coclosed, def:pet-ch9-de-rham-cohomology}\n  Every de Rham class on a closed oriented Riemannian manifold has exactly one\n  harmonic representative; equivalently,\n  $\\mathcal H^k(M)\\xrightarrow{\\sim}H^k(M)$.\n\\end{theorem}\n\\begin{proof}\n  \\uses{thm:pet-ch9-hodge-theorem,rem:pet-ch9-exercise-9-6-4,rem:pet-ch9-exercise-9-6-5}\n  \\sketch\n  The map is well defined and injective by\n  \\cref{lem:pet-ch9-harmonic-iff-closed-coclosed}.  Elliptic spectral theory,\n  developed in \\cref{rem:pet-ch9-exercise-9-6-4} and\n  \\cref{rem:pet-ch9-exercise-9-6-5}, yields\n  \\(\\Omega^k=\\operatorname{im}\\square\\oplus\\ker\\square\\).  Write a closed form as\n  \\(\\omega=d\\delta\\theta+\\delta d\\theta+\\widetilde\\omega\\), with\n  \\(\\square\\widetilde\\omega=0\\).  Applying \\(d\\) shows \\(d\\theta\\) is harmonic;\n  \\cref{lem:pet-ch9-harmonic-iff-closed-coclosed} then eliminates\n  \\(\\delta d\\theta\\).  Hence \\(\\omega\\) and \\(\\widetilde\\omega\\) are cohomologous.\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_TheBochnerTechnique.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_TheBochnerTechnique#def:pet-ch9-hodge-cohomology","title":"def:pet-ch9-hodge-cohomology","description":""},{"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_TheBochnerTechnique#lem:pet-ch9-harmonic-iff-closed-coclosed","title":"lem:pet-ch9-harmonic-iff-closed-coclosed","description":""},{"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_TheBochnerTechnique#def:pet-ch9-de-rham-cohomology","title":"def:pet-ch9-de-rham-cohomology","description":""},{"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_TheBochnerTechnique#rem:pet-ch9-exercise-9-6-4","title":"rem:pet-ch9-exercise-9-6-4","description":""},{"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_TheBochnerTechnique#rem:pet-ch9-exercise-9-6-5","title":"rem:pet-ch9-exercise-9-6-5","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}